PICS 0
BACnet Protocol Implementation Conformance Statement
Vendor Name: "Chipkin Automation Systems"
Product Name: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-SCHUB"
Product Model Number: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-SCHUB"
Product Description: "A BACnet Secure Connect hub built on the CAS BACnet Stack. BACnet/SC devices connect to it over TLS 1.3 WebSockets with mutual certificate authentication, and it relays their traffic. It can also connect out to another hub as a node (--sc-hub-uri). A BACnet/IP port for discovery and management is available when it is started with --port. Its certificates can be replaced over BACnet with the BACnet/SC certificate procedures."

BACnet Standardized Device Profiles Supported:
{
B-SCHUB - BACnet Secure Connect Hub
}

BIBBs Supported:
{
DS-RP-B
DS-RPM-B
DM-DDB-B
DM-DOB-B
DM-DCC-B
DM-TS-B
DM-UTC-B
NM-SCH-B
}

BACnet Standard Application Services Supported:
{
ReadProperty Execute
ReadPropertyMultiple Execute
WriteProperty Execute
AtomicReadFile Execute
AtomicWriteFile Execute
DeviceCommunicationControl Execute
ReinitializeDevice Execute
TimeSynchronization Execute
UTCTimeSynchronization Execute
IAm Initiate
IHave Initiate
WhoHas Execute
WhoIs Execute
}

Standard Object Types Supported:
{
Analog Input
Device
File
Network Port
}

Data Link Layer Option:
{
BACnet IP, (Annex J)
BACnet Secure Connect (Annex AB)
}

Character Sets Supported:
{
ISO 10646 (UTF-8) / ANSI X3.4
}

Special Functionality:
{
Maximum APDU size in octets: 1476
Segmented Requests Supported, window size: 1
Segmented Responses Supported, window size: 1
}

Default Property Value Restrictions:
{
unsigned-integer: <minimum: 0; maximum: 65535>
